{#
    A reference to one other record — the `join` alias.

    IT DELEGATES TO `select`, AND THAT IS THE POINT. Choosing one record out of a list and
    choosing one value out of a fixed list are the same act for the person doing it; only where
    the options come from differs, and that is already answered before this fragment runs
    (`RelationOptions`, ADR 0016 §2). Two files with the same markup would be two files to keep
    in step. It stays its own key because ADR 0013 keeps it apart: a project overriding the
    element for entity references must not change every fixed option list with it.

    `onejoin` NEVER ARRIVES HERE even though it shares this key. The core writes it through
    `doInsert`/`doUpdate` on the *target* record (`OnejoinType::toDatabase()`), so it is an owned
    sub-record and not a choice; `FormController::fragment()` sends it to `readonly`.
#}
